  "id": "Compound::DB01132 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Pioglitazone, a thiazolidinedione, is linked to Cyp2d6 through a shared pathway involving the PPAR gamma receptor. The evidence suggests that Pioglitazone, as part of the Thiazolidinediones class, binds to Rosiglitazone, which in turn interacts with Cyp2d6. This relationship is supported by the lowest common ancestor (LCA) structure, where Pioglitazone and Rosiglitazone both share a common ancestor in the Thiazolidinediones class, which also includes the antidiabetic agent category. The overlapping pathways through PPAR gamma further reinforce the connection, as Rosiglitazone is a PPAR gamma agonist. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, mechanistically linked relationship, where Pioglitazone's effects are mediated through the PPAR gamma receptor, leading to the activation of Cyp2d6. This integration highlights the role of PPAR gamma in modulating Cyp2d6 activity, underscoring the importance of receptor-mediated pathways in drug-target interactions.",
